# What ends up in the published package is primarily controlled by the
# "files": ["dist/"] field in package.json -- that's an allowlist and takes
# precedence over this file. This file is a second line of defense in case
# "files" is ever removed or broadened: nothing extra leaks into the tarball
# silently.
#
# Important: as long as this file exists, npm does NOT fall back to
# .gitignore when packing. So anything that shouldn't be published must be
# listed here explicitly, even if it's already in .gitignore.
#
# Syntax is the same as .gitignore. The "./" prefix doesn't work: use
# "tests", not "./tests".

# Tests and their configuration
tests/
jest.config.js
coverage/

# CI and local tooling configuration
.github/
.claude/

# Repo examples and assets: useful on GitHub, not needed by package consumers
examples/
assets/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.example

# Contributor docs: belong on GitHub, not in the tarball
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
todo.md

# npm already always includes package.json, README, LICENSE and the "main"
# entry file, and always excludes .git, node_modules, .npmrc and
# npm-debug.log -- no need to list them here.
